# UI Design Reference

When designing the LapGuard v2.0 UI, reference:
`/home/laptop/.cursor/reference/awesome-design-md/`

This repo contains DESIGN.md files (Google Stitch format) extracted from real product sites: color tokens, typography, components, layout, elevation, and do/don't rules.

## How to use

1. Do not copy a brand wholesale. Pick 1–2 closest systems and adapt tokens to LapGuard (battery/ops dashboard, loopback-first, safety-critical actions).
2. Read the chosen `design-md/<brand>/DESIGN.md` before generating UI.
3. Strong starting points for this product:
   - `linear.app` — dense, technical, dark, single accent
   - `posthog` / `sentry` — data-dense operator dashboards
   - `warp` / `supabase` — dark developer-tool chrome
   - `ibm` — structured enterprise system (Carbon-like)
4. Keep existing LapGuard safety UX: dry-run defaults, confirmation gates, no decorative danger.
